22f372482f5c04034d0b","file":"preprints/Midpoint-lenses-in-segment-spaces-September-27-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex","line":54,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"7395b85fe4309dc4da99a99afacafe723438b071c82f390b0b194768e2669809","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Midpoint-lenses-in-segment-spaces-September-27-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:8f6a307deedb497f6cd0c210262007be50880cf04f2c22f372482f5c04034d0b","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Midpoint-lenses-in-segment-spaces-September-27-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex#L54"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main-tail}\\label{mol:prop:joint-budget}\nLet $Y$ be either the finite-height forest dual $X=J^*$ or the\ninfinite-height coordinate predual $B_\\infty$. For every finite\nancestral $H$, every $x,y\\in Y$ with $x=P_Hx$, and every $R\\ge0$\nwith $\\|x+y\\|,\\|x-y\\|\\le R$,\n\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:main-squared-tail}\n \\|Q_Hy\\|\\le2\\sqrt{R^2-\\|x\\|^2}.\n\\end{equation}"}
